You are filling in missing facts and descriptions for authors on The Greatest Books, using the admin MCP server at <%= mcp_url %>. The "<%= type %>" enrichment queue holds <%= pending %> pending authors that our own model did not know well enough and that no Wikidata or library record was matched to. Work through all of them.

How to work the queue:

1. Call get_enrichment_queue with type "<%= type %>" once. `reference.answer_schema` is the exact shape of an answer: each fact is an object with a `value` and a `confidence` of high, medium or low.
2. Call claim_enrichment_items with type "<%= type %>". Keep `meta.lease_token`. The lease lasts 30 minutes, so claim only as many items as you can finish in that time: a `limit` of 5 suits web research.
3. For each item, read its `payload`: `record` is the author as we hold them, with their best-known books in our catalogue, and `tried` is what our own model already answered. The name may belong to several people: research only the person who wrote the books listed. Then research the author with your own web search.
4. Call submit_enrichment_item with the item's id, the lease token, your answer and the URLs you actually used as `sources`. Answer every key in the schema, with null (or an empty list) for a fact you did not find. Set `recognized` to true only when you are sure which person the item is; if you cannot tell who wrote these books, call skip_enrichment_item and say what you looked for.
5. Claim again. The queue is done only when a claim returns no items and `meta.remaining` is 0. If it returns no items but `meta.remaining` is above 0, claim again.

If submit_enrichment_item or skip_enrichment_item answers 409, the item is no longer yours (another worker took it, or your earlier call already went through). Drop it and move on.

If submit_enrichment_item answers 422, your answer did not match the schema. The item is still yours: fix the answer and submit again.

If either call answers 404, the item is gone: its author was deleted or merged into another. Drop it and move on.

Use sub-agents if you have them: each one runs steps 2 to 5 by itself. Two workers are never given the same author. A skipped item is never handed out again, so skip only after a real search.

The facts and the description, by the same rules our own model follows. Where they mention sources given below, read what you found on the web: no record of ours was matched to these authors.

<%= fact_rules %>

<%= description_rules %>

What is written. Submitting only fills blanks: a value the author already holds is never overwritten, and your answer for it is only recorded. An answer whose overall `confidence` is low is recorded and nothing is written. A fact you mark low is recorded and not written, so for a fact you are unsure of, give null rather than a guess, and do not raise your confidence to get an answer through. Nationalities are written only when the author has no country yet. A reviewer model checks the description before it is written: one that breaks the rules above is rewritten or dropped. Write it in your own words and never copy an encyclopedia's or a website's text. An author who already has a description written by our model keeps it.

You are authorised to act without asking me.

When you finish, call get_enrichment_queue once more and report its counts, then list the authors you skipped with one line each.
